@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Generated using the built-in image generation tool. All four calls used text only; no reference images.
+
+169
+Create one fresh image from text only, no reference image. Square 1024x1024.
+Use case: stylized-concept. Vintage engraved postage stamp, authentic intaglio print artwork.
+A single complete old postage stamp fills most of the square canvas, viewed perfectly straight on against plain aged ivory paper. Clearly visible perforated edges on all four sides. Fine ornamental engraved frame WITHOUT any text or numbers. Inside a small oval cameo, a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater is shown in elegant left-facing profile, happily lifting a tiny coffee cup to her lips. A croissant on a saucer is tucked into the lower cameo. Translate every character color into the engraving's SINGLE dark burgundy ink on ivory paper; no separately colored sweater or skin. Authentic postage-stamp proportions and simplified profile anatomy, exceptionally delicate tapered burin strokes, parallel curved hatching, fine crosshatching, tiny ink irregularities, tactile fibrous old paper. Ornamental scrollwork and floral details in the frame. An unmistakable faded circular postmark cancellation with a few wavy cancellation bars crosses one corner, composed ONLY of geometric ink lines with absolutely no lettering, dates or numbers. Flat printed artwork, not a photographic portrait with an engraving filter. The style fully dictates anatomy, framing and rendering. No text, captions, letters, numbers, signatures, or watermarks anywhere.
+
+170
+Generate one completely fresh image from text alone, with no reference images. Square 1024x1024.
+Use case: stylized-concept. Authentic intricate banknote engraving in green and violet ink on pale ivory cotton paper. A complete wide horizontal fantasy banknote centered within the square image, seen perfectly straight-on, with generous ivory margins above and below. Flat meticulously engraved security-print artwork, not a photo of a human and not a photograph with a filter. A radically asymmetrical banknote composition: a large finely engraved three-quarter-view portrait vignette on the right, and elaborate interlocking guilloche rosettes, looping spirographic medallions, ornamental ribbons and dense security line fields across the left and surrounding edges. The subject is a woman in her early 30s with shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee. Render all of her original colors entirely through the limited green and violet banknote inks. In this vignette her relaxed face tilts slightly down toward a steaming coffee cup cradled near her chest; her visible sweater has precise engraved knit stitches. A finely engraved croissant on a small plate forms a secondary still-life vignette at lower left, visually integrated into the guilloche ornaments. Exquisite steel-engraved crosshatching, dimensional curls defined only by engraved lines, little freckle dots, complex overlapping security patterns, microprint-like textures made ONLY of tiny abstract dashes and dots, subtle uneven ink pressure and cotton paper fibers. All blank spaces filled with abstract ornaments instead of bank names or denomination. Clearly banknote artistry, no real currency copied. No readable or unreadable lettering, no words, no digits, no numbers, no captions, no signature, no watermark.
+
+171
+Make one new image from text alone, no reference image. The final canvas MUST be square, width equals height, 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. A beautiful traditional Russian matryoshka folk-art still life: a handmade set of wooden nesting dolls representing the same woman, arranged in decreasing sizes on a wood tabletop. The woman is early 30s, has curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. Fully translate her into authentic matryoshka form: pear-shaped lathe-turned bodies, oversized flat painted round faces, rosy freckled cheeks, tiny stylized eyes behind painted tortoiseshell round spectacles, auburn spiral curls painted around the face, no naturalistic anatomy or separate limbs. Rich glossy lacquer over visible hand-painted brushwork. Mustard sweaters represented by decorative little painted knit chevrons around the shoulders and sleeves; deep red and dark green folk floral apron patterns with stylized daisies and berries, curved painted hands holding little white coffee cups, and golden croissants painted nearby on their aprons.
+Composition is a wide view of the ENTIRE doll set inside a SQUARE canvas with headroom, viewed from a slightly elevated three-quarter angle. The largest doll stands at rear left, followed by successively smaller complete dolls curving toward front right, so their sizes clearly decrease. One medium doll is OPEN: its hollow lower bowl stands in the front center showing unfinished pale wooden interior, with its matching painted upper half resting beside it on its side, opening visible. A tiny complete doll stands near the open shell, making the nesting idea unmistakable. A real small saucer with one croissant lies nearby on the tabletop. Soft warm daylight with rounded glossy reflections emphasizes tangible lacquer and wood, quiet muted background. The painted faces and bodies are emphatically folk-art stylizations, not realistic portraits applied to dolls. No text, letters, numbers, labels, captions, signatures or watermarks anywhere.
+
+172
+Create ONE brand new image from text only, no reference images. SQUARE canvas, 1024x1024, equal width and height.
+Use case: stylized-concept. A handcrafted ceramic tiki cocktail mug sculpted as a stylized woman's face, sitting on a bamboo tropical bar. The woman is early 30s with shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. Translate her completely into bold authentic tiki-mug ceramic sculpture: a squat cylindrical vessel with deeply carved, highly exaggerated angular cheeks, broad geometric nose, dramatically arched brows, heavy sculpted eyelids and a delighted stylized grin. Thick round raised ceramic tortoiseshell-pattern spectacles encircle the carved eyes. Auburn hair becomes chunky carved spiral coils wrapping both sides down to the shoulder/base. Freckles are small iron-oxide dots in the creamy face glaze. The lower part is a mustard-yellow sweater-shaped ceramic pedestal with deeply incised chunky chevron knit texture. Her tiny stylized hands and a small coffee cup are carved in relief on the lower front, integrating the enjoying-coffee motif into the object. Absolutely no realistic human skin and no real woman in the scene.
+The cup itself is OPEN at the top and filled with a tropical iced COFFEE cocktail: dark espresso-brown liquid and ice, a small bright turquoise paper cocktail umbrella, a bamboo straw and a small pineapple wedge. A golden croissant sits close beside the mug on a dark small plate.
+Use a dramatic close-up three-quarter view from just below the mug's eye level, offset within the frame, the whole mug and umbrella remain visible. Full sculptural depth, powerful asymmetrical carved features, thick glossy drip glaze pooled in grooves, amber and rust glazes running over mustard and cream, handmade ceramic irregularities and a tiny glaze crackle. Background: bamboo bar poles, palm-leaf shadows, dim tropical bar setting with warm amber lighting and restrained turquoise reflected highlights. Strong material presence, saturated lush colors, tactile ceramic craftsmanship; a crafted tiki face, not a realistic portrait printed on a cup. No text, letters, numbers, captions, logos, signatures or watermarks anywhere.
+

